VeridianOS: icccm: WM_CLASS class name stays within the property

Real bug, found while preparing 0002 for upstream
(gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/lib/libxcb-wm, issue #1). A WM_CLASS
property holding only an instance name whose terminator is the last
byte of the reply (e.g. "abc\0", no padding after it) made
xcb_icccm_get_wm_class_from_reply() point class_name one byte past the
end of the reply, so callers reading the class name read beyond it.
When nothing follows the instance name, the class name is now the empty
string at the instance name's terminator. Well-formed properties parse
as before.

--- a/icccm/icccm.c
+++ b/icccm/icccm.c
@@ -355,10 +355,12 @@
     prop->instance_name[len-1] = 0;
 
   name_len = strlen(prop->instance_name);
-  if(name_len == len)
-    name_len--;
-
-  prop->class_name = prop->instance_name + name_len + 1;
+  /* If nothing follows the instance name, the class name is empty: point
+     it at the terminator rather than past the end of the property. */
+  if(name_len >= len - 1)
+    prop->class_name = prop->instance_name + name_len;
+  else
+    prop->class_name = prop->instance_name + name_len + 1;
 
   return 1;
 }
